{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateParameter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.SubstrateParameter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_ne_one_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_ne_one_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L137-L141","doc":"In the strict quantum regime `q(p) > 1`, the substrate value is not\nclassical (`q(p) ≠ 1`); for real `q ≥ 1` this is exactly the\n\"not a root of unity\" condition ensuring semisimplicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.planck_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.planck_classical","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L132-L135","doc":"At `q(p) = 1` the Planck displacement vanishes (classicality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.planck_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.planck_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L126-L130","doc":"The Planck displacement is non-negative when `q(p) ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.planck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.planck","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L121-L124","doc":"The quantum Planck constant `ℏ_q(p) = 1 − q(p)⁻¹` measures\ndisplacement along the Reeb fibre.  At `q = 1`, `ℏ_q = 0`;\nas `q → ∞`, `ℏ_q → 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L117-L119","doc":"The interpolation coefficient `q(p)⁻¹` is well-defined: `q(p) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_pos","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L113-L115","doc":"The substrate field is strictly positive (from `q(p) ≥ 1 > 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.not_root_of_unity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.not_root_of_unity","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L107-L107","doc":"`q₀(p)` is never a root of unity.\n\nAdded to match the library declaration, which has carried it all along\nand whose consumers use it (bean `qou-6ome`). It is genuinely\nindependent of the classicality bound — `q = 1` satisfies `1 ≤ q` and\n*is* a root of unity — so it is a field rather than something the bound\nderives, unlike positivity.\n\nFlagged rather than adopted silently: `substrate-parameter.md` states the\nsubstrate parameter as `q ∈ End(𝟙)` and says nothing about roots of\nunity, so this is a library-side assumption the block does not yet\njustify. Whether the block should state it is an owner call. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_ge_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field_ge_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L94-L94","doc":"Classicality bound: `q(p) ≥ 1` at every point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.field","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L92-L92","doc":"The archimedean substrate field `q : M → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField.mk","kind":"ctor","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L90-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanSubstrateField","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L78-L107","doc":"**Archimedean substrate field**: the realisation of the substrate\nparameter as a genuine real field `q : M → ℝ` at and around the\nsubstrate value `q₀ ≈ 1.1097`, obtained by specialising the\ncategorical `R_q`-field through `ι : R_q → ℝ, q ↦ q₀`.\n\nIt carries the single archimedean axiom — the **classicality bound**\n`q(p) ≥ 1` — from which positivity, invertibility, and the\nnon-negativity of the quantum Planck displacement are derived.\n\n* `q(p) = 1` is the classical limit (`ℏ_q = 0`);\n* `q(p) > 1` is the quantum regime (the physical substrate sits here,\n  `q₀ ≈ 1.1097`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SubstrateParameter.field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SubstrateParameter.field","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L76-L76","doc":"The categorical substrate field `q : M → R_q`.\nRecords the local value of the `End(𝟙) ≅ R_q`-element at each\npoint `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SubstrateParameter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SubstrateParameter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SubstrateParameter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SubstrateParameter","kind":"structure","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L60-L76","doc":"**Substrate parameter** (categorical): the fibre coordinate `q ∈ k×`\non the one-parameter family of operators interpolating between\nthe full differential `d` and the vertical differential `π_V ∘ d`.\n\nWhen the quantum universe is fibred over a space `M`, the substrate\nparameter becomes a field `q : M → R_q`.  This is the **formal**\nmodulus field over the (un-ordered, non-field) ground ring `R_q`;\nthe archimedean properties (`q(p) > 0`, `q(p) ≥ 1`, not a root of\nunity) live on `ArchimedeanSubstrateField` below, after the\nsubstrate→archimedean wall (AGENTS.md §7c).\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:substrate-parameter}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:substrate-parameter","label":"def:substrate-parameter","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/substrate-parameter.lean#L54-L56","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}